{"name":"Snow White","hex":"#eeffee","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Snow White","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A fairy tale, the best-known version of Schneewittchen collected by the Brothers Grimm, in which a beautiful young girl is targeted by a jealous queen and tended by dwarfs.","The main character in that story."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Snow_White"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snow White","blocks":[{"text":"\"Snow White\" is a German fairy tale, first written down in the early 19th century. The Brothers Grimm published it in 1812 in the first edition of their collection Grimms' Fairy Tales, numbered as Tale 53. The original title was Sneewittchen, which is a partial translation from Low German. The modern spelling is Schneewittchen. The Grimms completed their final revision of the story in 1854, which can be found in the 1857 version of Grimms' Fairy Tales. The story was first published in English in 1823 under the title \"Snow-Drop\", which was also used in other early translations. Occasionally, the title \"Little Snow-White\" was also used."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Snow_White_and_the_Seven_Dwarfs_2.png/330px-Snow_White_and_the_Seven_Dwarfs_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow_White","wikidata":"Q11831"},{"title":"Snow White (2025 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Disney's Snow White, or simply Snow White, is a 2025 American musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Pictures. It is a live-action remake of Walt Disney's 1937 animated film Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs, itself based on the 1812 fairy tale. Directed by Marc Webb and written by Erin Cressida Wilson, the film stars Rachel Zegler as Snow White, with Andrew Burnap and Gal Gadot in supporting roles. The reimagined story follows the princess Snow White, who escapes assassination by her stepmother, the Evil Queen, and joins with seven magical beings of the forest and a rogue bandit named Jonathan to reclaim her kingdom."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1f/Snow_White_%282025_film%29_final_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow_White_(2025_film)","wikidata":"Q27660145"},{"title":"Snow","blocks":[{"text":"Snow is a form of solid atmospheric precipitation consisting of individual ice crystals that grow while suspended in the air—usually within clouds—and then fall, accumulating on the ground, where they undergo further changes. It consists of frozen crystalline water throughout its life cycle, starting when, under suitable conditions, the ice crystals form in the atmosphere, increase to millimeter size, precipitate and accumulate on surfaces, then metamorphose in place, and ultimately melt, slide, or sublimate away."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg/330px-CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow","wikidata":"Q7561"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Makart_hans_das_schlafende_schneewittchen.jpg/500px-Makart_hans_das_schlafende_schneewittchen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Makart_hans_das_schlafende_schneewittchen.jpg/500px-Makart_hans_das_schlafende_schneewittchen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The fable's antagonist the Evil Queen with the protagonist Snow White as depicted in The Sleeping Snow White by Hans Makart (1872)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMakart_hans_das_schlafende_schneewittchen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_1.jpg/120px-Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_1.jpg/250px-Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_1.jpg/120px-Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFranz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_2.jpg/120px-Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_2.jpg/250px-Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_2.jpg/120px-Franz_J%C3%BCttner_Schneewittchen_2.jpg?utm_